{
  "summary": "The change fixes the analyzer crash for [MessagePackObject(SuppressSourceGeneration = true)] types with invalid contracts: after reporting a mixed-key diagnostic it now skips the member, and duplicate-key dictionary inserts are guarded so duplicate keys no longer throw. All 8 new targeted analyzer/execution tests pass and the build passes. However, the same diff changes deserializing constructor parameter matching (`ctorParamIndex = 1`) for all types, breaking six previously-passing tests in the full suite, and the fail-without-fix check was not run, so the fix's test coverage is unverified and the change currently introduces regressions.",
  "requirement_verdicts": [
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-F1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "The contract-diagnostic tests for suppressed types pass (missing key MsgPack004, member type MsgPack003, allow-private MsgPack015), and the code still reports these diagnostics via reportDiagnostic; the fix keeps the analyzer from crashing while reporting them.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MemberWithoutKeyIsReported", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MemberTypeMustBeMessagePackObjectIsReported", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.AllowPrivateRequiredIsReported", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 929, "rev": "head", "quote": "Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.MemberNeedsKey, identifier?.GetLocation(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name);"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-F2",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "SourceGenerationOnlyDiagnosticsAreNotReportedWhenSuppressed passes, confirming that source-generation-only checks (partial-class, AOT-only) are not raised for a suppressed type.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.SourceGenerationOnlyDiagnosticsAreNotReportedWhenSuppressed", "outcome": "passed"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-N1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "The three WithoutAnalyzerFailure tests (duplicate int keys, duplicate string keys, mixed key kinds) pass on head, demonstrating the analyzer no longer crashes on invalid contracts for suppressed types; the full-suite failures are unrelated constructor/generation regressions covered in finding N1.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.DuplicateIntKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.DuplicateStringKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MixedKeyKindsAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1008, "rev": "head", "quote": "continue; // The key kind does not match the other members; the diagnostic is reported, so skip this member."},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1023, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (!intMembers.ContainsKey(member.IntKey))"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-N2",
      "verdict": "not_met",
      "confidence_basis": "tests.fail_without_fix was not run, so 'tests fail without the fix' is unverified, and the full suite shows six new failures (regressions), violating 'no regressions in the existing test suite'.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "N1",
      "title": "Change breaks six previously-passing tests (regression)",
      "severity": "blocker",
      "category": "correctness",
      "claim": "The full suite reports six tests that pass on base but fail on head (GenerationTests.DeserializingConstructorParameterMemberTypeAssignability_Incompatible, GenerationTests.DeserializingConstructorParameterMemberTypeAssignability_MemberAssignsToParamType, GenerationTests.NoPrivateAccessNeeded, GenerationTests.NonDefaultDeserializingConstructor_Private, MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.AddAttributeToTypeForRecordPrimaryConstructor, MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.AddAttributesToMembersOfRecordWithPrimaryCtor). This violates REQ-2234-N2's 'no regressions' and blocks merging. The likely cause is the constructor-parameter index change (`ctorParamIndex = 1` at head line 1241 vs `0` at base line 1227), which alters deserializing-constructor matching for all types, not just SuppressSourceGeneration types.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1241, "rev": "head", "quote": "var ctorParamIndex = 1;"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1227, "rev": "base", "quote": "var ctorParamIndex = 0;"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Revert or scope the ctorParamIndex change, then re-run the full suite and tests.fail_without_fix before merging."
    },
    {
      "id": "N2",
      "title": "fail_without_fix check was not run; fix coverage unverified",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "tests",
      "claim": "REQ-2234-N2 requires automated tests that fail without the fix, but tests.fail_without_fix was not executed (listed in not_run). The new targeted tests pass on head, but their fail-without-fix behavior is unconfirmed, so the coverage requirement cannot be verified.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MemberWithoutKeyIsReported", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.DuplicateIntKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "passed"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Run tests.fail_without_fix (source-reverted) to confirm the new tests fail without the fix."
    }
  ],
  "refusals": [
    {
      "topic": "Precise root cause of the six full-suite failures",
      "reason": "Attributing the regressions definitively to the ctorParamIndex change would require running fail-without-fix or targeted regression tests, which were not executed; the change is the only difference between base and head, so the link is strong but not test-confirmed.",
      "who_should_decide": "Area owner / change author",
      "req": "REQ-2234-N2",
      "blocking": false
    }
  ],
  "refutations": []
}
